From fdf7b97c99142698dd59d365aae3b7e65c6b1fe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:38:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] code skew: a checkout move over tests/docs/CI
 commits only is no skew (RESTART_IGNORE_GLOBS)

hermes-hub applies every main commit within minutes and restarted the gateway and every serve
backend on each apply: 78 restarts in 3 h for 129 commits on 2026-11-13, 28 of them touching
only tests, docs or CI. hermes_cli/restart_ignore_paths.py holds the one exact list
(tests/**, docs/**, .github/**, top-level README*/CONTRIBUTING*/SECURITY*, .mailmap; never
*.md in general: SKILL.md, AGENTS.md, SOUL.md and prompts are runtime inputs) and
range_restart_free(): a strict-ancestor range whose every commit (merges against each parent)
touches only those paths. detect_code_skew() treats such a drift as no skew, so no
'Restart required', skew retirement or update-pause skew release fires for it. hermes-sync
reads the tuple from HEAD to fast-forward such ranges without a restart (t_01a1d471b754e5bc).
---
 gateway/code_skew.py                          |  28 +++-
 hermes_cli/restart_ignore_paths.py            |  84 ++++++++++
 tests/hermes_cli/test_restart_ignore_paths.py | 145 ++++++++++++++++++
 tests/hermes_cli/test_web_server_skew_exit.py |  33 ++++
 4 files changed, 289 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 hermes_cli/restart_ignore_paths.py
 create mode 100644 tests/hermes_cli/test_restart_ignore_paths.py

